    <string name="tips_for_android12">Android 12 and newer kill the background processes this virtual system needs, so it may fail to boot.\n\nTo fix it (no root needed):\n1. Settings → About phone → tap \"Build number\" 7 times to enable Developer options.\n2. Open Developer options and turn ON \"Disable child process restrictions\".\n3. Come back and start the app again.\n\nIf your phone has no such option, connect it to a PC and run:\nadb shell settings put global settings_enable_monitor_phantom_procs false</string>
